 "about": "One row per data set. Every range is read from the data, never typed in: the observed spectrum from its own file, ours from the promoted run summaries (a fitted window, a window with no telluric line above the cut, or one that failed), and the others' from their corrected columns, with the pixels they interpolated or drew by hand left out (photatl's ``atmospheric < dg``, niratl's -1.0 fill, Kurucz's straight stretches, Wallace 2011's blanks below T = 0.8). ACE-FTS is observed from orbit, so it is telluric-free over its whole range rather than corrected. Coverage is decided on 1 cm-1 bins: a bin counts when more than half of its pixels are valid.",
